WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.067 line:92%
-Our first guest tonight i

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:03.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
a Grammy-nominated
country-music superstar,

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:03.803 line:92%
and coach on "The Voice."

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:07.440
The season finale airs
this Monday and Tuesday at 8:00,

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
here on NBC.
Let's take a look.

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:10.944 line:92%
-Blake, let me go with you, bud.

00:00:10.944 --> 00:00:12.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What -- Where is the --
What camera?

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:14.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
What camera am I looking in?
-Just talk to America.

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:17.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
-America, this show is
called "The Voice."

00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:22.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
When have you ever in your lif
heard a voice like that?

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:23.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.
-Recognize it.

00:00:23.757 --> 00:00:25.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So great.
-And reward it!

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:26.426 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.426 --> 00:00:28.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Please welcome back
to the show Blake Shelton.

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:31.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
How are you, Blake?
-Hey, Seth, you know what?

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:33.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was watching that clip
right there.

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:35.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
By the way, hello.
Good to see you.

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:39.172
But I just was reminded becaus
you came from the "SNL" world,

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:44.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was channeling my best
Chris Farley and Adam Sandler.

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:46.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
Remember The Herlihy boy?
-Absolutely.

00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:48.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Let the boy
babysit your grandma!"

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:51.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
"He's a good boy!"

00:00:51.351 --> 00:00:52.419 line:92%
-That's right, that's right.

00:00:52.419 --> 00:00:57.490
-I had your beautiful fiancée --
Gwen was on the show in October.

00:00:57.490 --> 00:01:00.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have a --
I have a small gripe,

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:02.829 line:92%
which is, the very next day,

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:04.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
she basically announced
on Instagram

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:07.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you guys had been engaged
That's the kind of content

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:09.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
we could have really had
a lot of fun with.

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:12.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
Why did she wait
until the day she left?

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:15.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I remember this,
by the way, Seth,

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:18.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
because she did
your show from --

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:20.413 line:92%
I believe she was in Oklahoma.

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:23.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have a little cabin there
that we stay in.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.351 line:92%
And believe it or not, somehow

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:26.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
I figured out how to get
Internet there.

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:30.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she -- And she kept, like,
doing this with her hand

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:33.860
and, you know, wondering
if people would figure out

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:35.495 size:75% position:38%
that she was wearing
an engagement ring.

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:37.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I told her --
I said, "You know,

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:40.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
you wear more jewelry
than Mr. T.,

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:44.304
so I don't think anybody
is gonna pick up on that, Gwen."

00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:46.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And they didn't.

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:47.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
You could have figured it out,
though.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:48.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
She was giving you hints.
-I know.

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:52.312
It's very hard over Zoom,
because you never know.

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:53.012 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I don't want to stare.

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:56.349
You end up looking in the camera
more than you do at the guests

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:57.317 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So it was true.

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:58.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was right in front of me,
and I missed it.

00:01:58.585 --> 00:02:00.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't want to ask too much
about wedding plans.

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:05.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it does strike me
that with the two of you,

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:08.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
picking a wedding band
has very --

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:09.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I'm assuming
you know a lot of people,

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:12.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
but that's a high-pressure gig
to be the wedding band

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:14.701 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
at your shindig.

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:17.303 line:92%
-You know, I've kind of decide

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:22.475
that, you know, I've been
doing this a long time now

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:24.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I've got a lot of favors
out there.

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:26.446 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And he may not like it,

00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:30.750
but Adam Levine is going t
have to get the band togethe

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.051 line:92%
and come and play our wedding.

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:35.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think that would be --
I've already seen a music vide

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:37.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
where they crash
people's weddings.

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:39.959 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And he owes me, a lot,

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:41.861 align:start size:94% position:6%
for just putting up with him
over the years.

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:43.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
So maybe we can get Adam
to come be our wedding band.

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:46.065
Not "maybe." We are going to
-I think he should do that

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:48.268 size:84% position:42%
And while he's playing,
I think you and Gwen

00:02:48.268 --> 00:02:51.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
should turn your chairs around
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:53.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, I like that idea.
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:53.106 --> 00:02:55.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And plus, their music
is so boring,

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:58.278 size:81% position:41%
that it won't distract
from the festivities

00:02:58.278 --> 00:02:59.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the reception
and all that stuff.

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:02.415
-Right, you should maybe hav
them play in a separate barn

00:03:02.415 --> 00:03:06.286
You know, like you can go over
if you want to relax a little.

00:03:06.286 --> 00:03:08.054 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:10.924 line:92%
You and Gwen also just release

00:03:10.924 --> 00:03:13.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
your second number-one singl
together.

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:16.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
When we were here,
we were talking about the fact

00:03:16.196 --> 00:03:18.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you guys won a CMT Award.
-Yeah.

00:03:18.965 --> 00:03:20.533 line:92%
-And now, obviously, you know,

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:22.902 size:84% position:42%
you have introduced her
to your genre of music.

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:26.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
It would be fun, and
I think your fans would enjoy,

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:28.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
just one ska song.
Just one.

00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:30.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I knew that's where
you were going with this.

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:33.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
Can you imagine?
I don't even know.

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:37.650 size:81% position:41%
I'm not even certain
what "ska" even means.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:40.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, is that like a --
Is that a genre?

00:03:40.687 --> 00:03:43.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that just a...
-Yeah, I would say,

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:46.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's sort of reggae-inspired
genre of music.

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:49.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think it's, like,
right in your wheelhouse.

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:52.999
-You know, maybe I could -
I don't even know, actually.

00:03:52.999 --> 00:03:55.868
I was starting to say, maybe I
could get away with some reggae.

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I still don't think
I could perform.

00:03:57.937 --> 00:03:59.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Chuckles ]
-Yeah.

00:03:59.105 --> 00:04:02.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did not know this about you
and I apologize,

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:04.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you're producing
a Hallmark movie.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.178 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
This is your third.

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:08.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the part about it
that's fascinating to me -

00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:11.451
it's a Christmas film -- you
produced it with your mother

00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:13.353 line:92%
-[ Chuckling ] That's true

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:15.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
That is fascinating,
isn't it, Seth?

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:17.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
I will say I love my mother.

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:19.926
I don't know if I would love
to produce a film with her

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:22.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
Especially a holiday film.
-The joys of working

00:04:22.095 --> 00:04:24.897 size:84% position:42%
with your mom in the
entertainment industry.

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:27.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
What happened was,
we wrote a song together.

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:31.904
I had a Christmas album that
came out several years ago

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:37.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
And my mom is a little bit
like Lucy Ricardo,

00:04:37.477 --> 00:04:41.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
where she's
constantly harassing Ricky

00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:44.717
to let her be on the show, o
let her sing or write a song

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:46.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
My mom has always
wanted to be a songwriter.

00:04:46.319 --> 00:04:51.090
So she's always texting me o
talking to me about song ideas

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:53.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, finally, one day,
I said, "Look,

00:04:53.159 --> 00:04:56.129
I'm making a Christmas album
I think it would be appropriat

00:04:56.129 --> 00:05:00.133
for you and I to finally write
this Christmas song together

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:01.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll record it.
It'll be on my album,

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:05.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we'll sing it like a duet.
And so we did this thing.

00:05:05.538 --> 00:05:08.875 line:92%
And then, they ended up --

00:05:08.875 --> 00:05:10.810 line:92%
Some publisher came along,

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:14.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
and offered her a book dea
because of this song.

00:05:14.347 --> 00:05:15.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, because
the book came out,

00:05:15.882 --> 00:05:17.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
then the Hallmark Channel
came along

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:20.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they offered to do a movie
based on the book.

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:24.657
And the movie did good, an
here we are, three movies later.

00:05:24.657 --> 00:05:26.559 size:75% position:38% line:92%
So, just let me know

00:05:26.559 --> 00:05:28.695
if you want to do any work
with any family members.

00:05:28.695 --> 00:05:31.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you, um --
I do want to ask real quic

00:05:31.798 --> 00:05:32.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
about this season
of "The Voice."

00:05:32.932 --> 00:05:35.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
Coming in the homestretch,
you seem pretty well-positione

00:05:35.702 --> 00:05:39.505
to take the crown again.
Are you feeling confident?

00:05:39.505 --> 00:05:42.408 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Sighs ] I am.

00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:47.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, the problem
for Team Blake this year,

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:48.281 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I have two members left,

00:05:48.281 --> 00:05:50.616 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is incredible
in the finale.

00:05:50.616 --> 00:05:52.251 line:92%
Everybody else just has one.

00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:57.857
But Gwen happens to have thi
very, very special young man

00:05:57.857 --> 00:06:00.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
named Carter Rubin,
that I feel like,

00:06:00.993 --> 00:06:03.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
if there's a threat to all o
our teams, it's that kid.

00:06:03.596 --> 00:06:08.267
And if he wins, I don't thin
any of us would be mad about it,

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:10.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
because he deserves it,
he's a special kid.

00:06:10.636 --> 00:06:15.408
But my team has been strong,
and they have been all season.

00:06:15.408 --> 00:06:17.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we never know
how the voting is going.

00:06:17.377 --> 00:06:19.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
They never clue us in.
You would think,

00:06:19.212 --> 00:06:22.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
after almost 20 seasons
of doing this show,

00:06:22.081 --> 00:06:25.551
I could pull some favors,
but I still never know

00:06:25.551 --> 00:06:27.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
what's going on
behind the scenes.

00:06:27.153 --> 00:06:30.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I would say Carter
is going to be

00:06:30.056 --> 00:06:32.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
our toughest competition,
all of us coaches,

00:06:32.959 --> 00:06:36.596
'cause he's a special -- he'
got a pretty decent coach, too

00:06:36.596 --> 00:06:39.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, it's incredible
to watch

00:06:39.499 --> 00:06:41.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
the talent of the singers
on the show,

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:43.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I'm always taken, as well,
with the amount of nerve

00:06:43.669 --> 00:06:46.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
they need to have to go ou
and perform live,

00:06:46.739 --> 00:06:48.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
in front of --
even without an audience,

00:06:48.975 --> 00:06:52.812
they're performing in front of
these four -- the four of you.

00:06:52.812 --> 00:06:54.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you think you would have ha
the confidence

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:56.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
to go out there at their age
and do what they do?

00:06:56.482 --> 00:07:01.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, Seth, I honestly --
I think it's probably --

00:07:01.487 --> 00:07:03.723 line:92%
I put myself in their position

00:07:03.723 --> 00:07:06.058 line:92%
And no different than, you know,

00:07:06.058 --> 00:07:07.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
how you're having to do
this show now,

00:07:07.493 --> 00:07:11.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
things are, I feel like,
easier if you have an audience

00:07:11.531 --> 00:07:15.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
versus four people
sitting out there,

00:07:15.768 --> 00:07:17.804 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and you get the...

00:07:17.804 --> 00:07:19.372 line:92%
You know, no matter what you do,

00:07:19.372 --> 00:07:21.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
it sounds like
it was disastrous.

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:22.542 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-[ Chuckling ] Right.

00:07:22.542 --> 00:07:24.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We are in entertainment,
you know,

00:07:24.277 --> 00:07:26.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there's
no immediate feedback.

00:07:26.212 --> 00:07:27.947 line:92%
There's nobody to go high-five

00:07:27.947 --> 00:07:32.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I think it's actually
harder this way.

00:07:32.084 --> 00:07:34.720 line:92%
When I was a kid, you know

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:37.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would get stage fright
to get onstage.

00:07:37.657 --> 00:07:38.491 size:88% position:44% line:92%
But once I got up there,

00:07:38.491 --> 00:07:40.226 size:75% position:38%
and I could can hear
some singing along

00:07:40.226 --> 00:07:42.662 size:75% position:38%
or see some smiling,
I kinda got over it.

00:07:42.662 --> 00:07:47.533
So, I really feel for them
the way we're doing it now

00:07:47.533 --> 00:07:49.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like it's
even more awkward

00:07:49.502 --> 00:07:53.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
than, you know, getting onstag
in front of 2,000 people,

00:07:53.606 --> 00:07:57.043 align:start size:94% position:6%
or however many we have
in our audience normally -

00:07:57.043 --> 00:07:58.177 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
400, I think.

00:07:58.177 --> 00:08:00.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it's
a special group of people.

00:08:00.379 --> 00:08:01.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's always a delight
to talk to you.

00:08:01.981 --> 00:08:03.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thanks so much
for being here, Blake.

00:08:03.516 --> 00:08:04.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You too, buddy.
Good to see you.

00:08:04.617 --> 00:08:09.489
Have you had a chance to talk to
Brad Paisley in a while?

00:08:09.489 --> 00:08:10.523 line:92%
I know you guys are buddies.

00:08:10.523 --> 00:08:13.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, you know,
we stay in touch via text.

00:08:13.226 --> 00:08:14.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know he's probably
a lot like you.

00:08:14.494 --> 00:08:16.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's just itching to
get back out there on the road

00:08:16.329 --> 00:08:19.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
A guy who really likes being
in front of his audience.

00:08:19.532 --> 00:08:21.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
Worked really hard
to get that audience,

00:08:21.734 --> 00:08:23.603
and it's a shame that he's not
performing in front of them.

00:08:23.603 --> 00:08:27.340
-Tell him I said, "Kiss my ass,"
next time you talk to him.

00:08:27.340 --> 00:08:29.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Appreciate that.

00:08:29.375 --> 00:08:30.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The season finale of
"The Voice"

00:08:30.409 --> 00:08:32.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
airs Monday and Tuesday
at 8:00 on NBC.

00:08:32.645 --> 00:08:35.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
We will be right back
with Jenny Slate.

